# Test: the daemon refuses to start on a config a registered validator rejects.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-config-validators-bypassed-at-startup AC-1 -- a value a
#            ze:validate custom validator refuses stops `ze` at load. The daemon
#            exits 1, names the section, the leaf and the rule, and binds
#            nothing, so the value reaches no protocol encoder.
# PREVENTS:  the regression this spec closes. Until 2026-08-11 LoadConfig parsed
#            and returned, and ValidateTreeAllModules had exactly one non-test
#            caller (`ze config validate`), so every custom validator was
#            bypassed at daemon start and at SIGHUP. A hand-edited config
#            reached the wire unvalidated.
#
# The value below passes the YANG schema on its own: the `use` leaf is
# `type string { length "1..64" }`, so nothing but the custom validator can
# refuse it. That is what makes this test discriminate -- revert the
# ValidateCustomSections call in LoadConfig and the refusal disappears.
#
# The enforcing producer is InternalPluginNameValidator
# (internal/component/config/validators.go), reached through the ze:validate
# extension on plugin/internal/use in
# internal/component/plugin/yang/ze-plugin-conf.yang, walked by
# ValidateCustomSections (internal/component/config/validate_sections.go).

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	internal p1 {
		use no-such-plugin-exists
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=config:exit=1:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=config validation failed
expect=stderr:contains=plugin
expect=stderr:contains=no-such-plugin-exists
expect=stderr:contains=is not a registered internal plugin

# The same config through `ze config validate` refuses identically. Both
# callers run one walk over one section list, so an operator who checks a
# config before an upgrade learns exactly what the daemon will do with it.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config:exit=1
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=is not a registered internal plugin
